Spec: Conference entity

Purpose:
  The Conference entity: a date and a title, marking a one-day event such as a conference, a workshop or a seminar
  that the teacher attends or presents at. It carries no Semester or Course reference, so one entry speaks for the
  whole calendar, and it never blocks teaching: it coexists with a Holiday and with the Lessons of that day, since
  the teacher may still teach on it. A conference spanning several days is stored as one Conference per day. A
  view-less, route-less package used by ../semester/semester.sdd, ../realizations/realizations.sdd,
  ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd and ../mcp_server/mcp_server.sdd.

Owns:
  ./__init__.py
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Must:
  A Conference has a date and a title. Its date is indexed for range listings.
  A date carries at most one Conference, held the same way as ../holidays/holidays.sdd holds its one Holiday per date:
    @ConferenceService.add_conference rejects a date that already holds one with @DuplicateConferenceError,
    @ConferenceService.update_conference re-checks it while ignoring the Conference being edited, and a unique index
    on the table's date enforces it for a write that bypasses the service. A Conference therefore spans exactly one
    day, per ./conferences.sdd's Purpose.
  A Conference has no foreign key: it is global to the calendar, like a Holiday, and not owned by a Semester or a
    Course.
  A Conference never blocks teaching: no use case checks its date against a Semester's NoTeachWeeks or a day's
    Lessons, so storing one leaves that day's Lessons in place.
  @ConferenceService.add_conference rejects an empty title with @InvalidConferenceError before storage.
  @ConferenceService.update_conference applies the same title check as @ConferenceService.add_conference and
    rejects an unknown id with @UnknownConferenceError.
  @ConferenceService.delete_conference removes one Conference, rejecting an unknown id with @UnknownConferenceError.
  @ConferenceRepository in ./ports.py exposes operations to get, list Conferences for a date range, and to add,
    update and delete one.
  The table is created automatically on startup when it does not exist, and its unique date index replaces an earlier
    non-unique index of the same name instead of leaving the constraint absent.
  A Conference's title is content the teacher reads and edits rather than UI text, so it is stored as entered; the
    English sentence the views show about a Conference is UI text and lives in their view.py, per /aikana.sdd.

Must not:
  This package must not gain a view.py or routes.py: a Conference is created, edited and removed through
    ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd's Conference tab, so those affordances and routes stay owned there.

Scenario: A Conference leaves the day's Lessons in place
  Given a day holds a Lesson of some CourseRealization
  When the admin adds a Conference on that day
  Then the day's row shows both the Lesson square and the Conference's title

Scenario: The admin edits the Conference already on the clicked date
  Given a Conference is stored on a date the admin clicks in ../semester/semester.sdd's wall planner
  When the admin opens the dialog's Conference tab and changes the title or the date
  Then the new date shows the new title and the previous one no longer shows it

Scenario: Two Conferences on one date are rejected
  Given a Conference is stored on a date
  When the admin adds another Conference on that same date
  Then the stored one is left as it was and the dialog reports the rejection

Tasks:
  [x] Implement @Conference in ./domain.py and the @ConferenceRepository-backed ./ports.py, ./services.py and
    ./repository_sqlite.py, holding the one-Conference-per-date rule with a unique index, per ../architecture.sdd